# Supabase (Phase 2 persistence). Copy to .env and set values.
# Get these from Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Solicitor "Continue with Microsoft 365" (Azure OAuth via Supabase). Set to "false" to hide the button.
# Enable the Azure provider in Supabase → Authentication → Providers, and in Azure add redirect:
#   https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
# In Supabase → URL Configuration, add your app redirect, e.g.:
#   http://localhost:5173/celista-login  and  https://your-domain/celista-login
# VITE_MICROSOFT_SIGNIN_ENABLED=true
#
# Client questionnaire: show "Auto-Fill Form (Test Data)" on hosted prod (default hidden for real clients). Uncomment for demos only:
# VITE_SHOW_CLIENT_AUTOFILL=true
#
# If Microsoft login shows "Unable to exchange external code" (Supabase, not this app):
#   Entra ID → Your app → Authentication: add https://<project>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback as **Web** (not SPA).
#   Supabase → Providers → Azure: Client ID, Secret **Value** (new secret if expired; not Secret ID), Tenant URL
#   https://login.microsoftonline.com/<Directory tenant ID>
#
# Microsoft calendar connection requests these delegated Microsoft Graph permissions:
#   User.Read, Calendars.ReadBasic, offline_access
# Add Calendars.ReadBasic to the Entra app API permissions and grant admin consent if user consent is disabled.
#
# Optional: browser telemetry for auth/support (no passwords logged). solicitors also use login page → “Copy sign-in diagnostics”.
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://...@....ingest.sentry.io/...
# Admins correlate failures with Supabase Dashboard → Logs → Auth (OAuth / token exchange).
#
# Sign-in log (solicitor nav): comma-separated emails that see **Sign-in log** — not every user with profiles.role admin.
# If unset, defaults to SOLICITOR_ADMIN_OVERRIDE_EMAIL hardcoded in `src/lib/auth.js`.
# VITE_SIGN_IN_LOG_ALLOW_EMAILS=you@aristonesolicitors.co.uk

# Optional: set to "true" to enable verbose [BUILD CLAUSES], [INTERPOLATE], and [CONDITION EVAL] console logs (default: off).
# VITE_DEBUG_CLAUSES=true
